<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Igara</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1901 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small kingdom of western Uganda, merged into the Kingdom of Ankole under British rule in 1901.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Igara lay in the hills west of today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushenyi-district">Bushenyi</a>, between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-buhweju">Buhweju</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Kingdom of Ankole</a>. It emerged as a separate state in the 18th century, with a royal line remembered in local tradition. Little is reliably known of its early history.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Igara was a farming and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-keeping kingdom, governed by a king with clan heads and drums of office in the manner of its neighbours. It was often drawn into the wars between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Ankole</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro">Bunyoro</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankole-agreement">Ankole Agreement</a> of 1901 merged Igara into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Kingdom of Ankole</a> as one of its counties. It is now part of western Uganda's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bushenyi-district">Bushenyi</a> area.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1700 CE – 1901 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1901 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Runyankole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Uganda</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Igara</dd></dl></aside></div>
